PART 4: BLOOMBERG 5-STAGE SYSTEM DESIGN QUESTION BANK
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Standard 5-Stage Framework:
Stage 01: Clarify (Scope, Functional/Non-Functional Reqs, Out-of-Scope)
Stage 02: Interactions (Client Actions, Complete REST/gRPC APIs, Status Codes)
Stage 03: Identify Data (Relational Schema, PK/FK, Invariants, ACID Rationale)
Stage 04: Draw Simple Design (Client <-> Service <-> SQL Database; No premature scale)
Stage 05: Challenge & Improve (Bottlenecks, Caching, Invalidation, Concurrency, Failures)

================================================================================
QUESTION 1: ROOM BOOKING SYSTEM (Official Bloomberg Workshop Question)
================================================================================
Stage 01: Clarify
- Functional Reqs: Filter rooms (building, capacity, facilities); reserve time slot;
  cancel booking; view my bookings.
- Non-Functional Reqs: Latency < 50ms for search; zero double-booking (strong consistency).
- Out of Scope: Payments, recurring series, badge IoT access.

Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)
- GET /rooms?building={b}&min_capacity={c}&facilities={f}&start_time={t1}&end_time={t2}
- GET /rooms/{id} -> Room details
- GET /me/bookings -> List current user bookings
- POST /bookings -> Body: {room_id, start_time, end_time}. Returns: {booking_id, status: CONFIRMED}
- DELETE /bookings/{id} -> Returns: 204 No Content

Stage 03: Data Model (PostgreSQL / Relational)
- users: user_id (PK), name, email, department
- rooms: room_id (PK), building, capacity, facilities (ARRAY/JSON), is_active
- bookings: booking_id (PK), user_id (FK), room_id (FK), start_time (TIMESTAMP),
  end_time (TIMESTAMP), status (Enum: PENDING, CONFIRMED, CANCELLED)
- Domain Invariant: No overlapping active bookings for the same room:
  EXCLUDE USING gist (room_id WITH =, tsrange(start_time, end_time) WITH &&)
  WHERE (status = 'CONFIRMED')

Stage 04: Simple Design
- Client App <---> Booking Service <---> PostgreSQL Database
- Booking Service runs validation, SQL transactions, and availability queries.

Stage 05: Challenge & Improve
- Bottleneck: Frequent room search queries overload database reads.
- Mitigation: Redis cache for static room metadata and precomputed availability bitsets.
- Cache Invalidation: Invalidate affected room-date search cache keys on booking create/cancel.
- Concurrency / Double Booking: Concurrent booking attempts for same room-time slot handled
  via DB transaction with SELECT FOR UPDATE or PostgreSQL exclusion constraint.

