QUESTION 4: BUILD CACHE (CI/CD Acceleration)
================================================================================
Stage 01: Clarify
- Functional Reqs: Check if input signature is already built; download pre-built binary
  artifact; upload new artifact on cache miss.
- Non-Functional Reqs: Cache lookup < 20ms; multi-gigabit throughput; cryptographic correctness.
- Out of Scope: Compiling source code (handled by build runners).

Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)
- GET /v1/artifacts/{hash_key} -> Stream binary blob (200 OK) or 404 Not Found.
- PUT /v1/artifacts/{hash_key} -> Upload binary artifact stream with metadata.

Stage 03: Data Model & Invariants
- Content-Addressed Hash: hash_key = SHA256(source_code_files + compiler_version + flags + env_deps)
- Artifact Metadata Table (PostgreSQL):
  * hash_key (PK, CHAR(64)), artifact_size_bytes (BIGINT), s3_storage_uri (VARCHAR),
    created_at (TIMESTAMP), last_accessed_at (TIMESTAMP)
- Storage Tier: Raw binary blobs stored in distributed Blob Storage (S3 / Ceph).

Stage 04: Simple Design
- Build Agent <---> Cache Service (Metadata Lookup) <---> Blob Storage (S3) + PostgreSQL DB.

Stage 05: Challenge & Improve
- Eviction Policy: LRU paired with TTL (evict artifacts not requested in 20 days).
- Consistent Hashing: Shard local fast NVMe SSD edge storage servers using consistent
  hash ring with virtual nodes for high-throughput streaming.
- Cache Stampede: Mutex locking / single-flight pattern: when 50 jobs build the exact
  same commit simultaneously, only 1 job builds and 49 await the cached artifact.

