QUESTION 7: NEWS FEED / MOST READ ARTICLES
================================================================================
Stage 01: Clarify
- Functional Reqs: Ingest click events; return Top-K articles; support rolling windows (1h, 24h).
- Non-Functional Reqs: Non-blocking ingestion; get_most_read_articles() latency < 20ms.

Stage 02: Interactions (APIs)
- Event Ingestion: POST /events/read -> Request body: {article_id, user_id, timestamp}
- Read API: GET /articles/trending?window=24h&limit=10 -> Returns: [{"article_id": "art_10", "reads": 45200}]

Stage 03: Data Model
- raw_reads: article_id, timestamp (Ingested to stream/Kafka, not directly to SQL).
- aggregated_counts: article_id, time_bucket (1-minute slice), read_count.
- Storage: Redis Sorted Sets (ZSET) for real-time Top-K ranking: ZREVRANGEBYSCORE.

Stage 04: Simple Design
- Client App -> Event Ingest Service -> Buffer Queue -> Aggregator -> Redis Sorted Set -> API Server.

Stage 05: Challenge & Improve
- Sliding-Window Aggregation: Dividing 24 hours into 1,440 1-minute buckets. Background
  worker maintains rolling count by adding the newest minute and evicting the oldest minute.
- Cache Invalidation & Heavy Write Load: Never write directly to database per click.
  Batch events in memory at ingestion layer (flush every 1,000 events or 1 second)
  and execute atomic Redis increments: ZINCRBY trending_24h 1 {article_id}.
- Cold Cache Recovery: Periodically snapshot top-K rankings to PostgreSQL every 5 minutes.
